[42.567, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mSecurity Audit Report\u001b[m\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m1. SQL Injection (Critical)\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mVulnerability\u001b[m: The \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mgetUserByName\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m and \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mlogin\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m functions in \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33msrc/users.js\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m use string concatenation to build SQL queries.\r\n- \u001b[1mExample\u001b[m: \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mconst sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '\" + name + \"'\";\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mImpact\u001b[m: An attacker can bypass authentication or extract sensitive data from the database by injecting SQL commands into the\r\n\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mname\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33muser\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, or \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mpass\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m parameters.\r\n- \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Use parameterized queries (prepared statements) provided by the \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmysql\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m library.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m2. Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) (High)\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mVulnerability\u001b[m: The \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mgetUserByName\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m function reflects the \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mname\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m query parameter directly into the HTML response without\r\nsanitization.\r\n- \u001b[1mExample\u001b[m: \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mres.send('Resu"]
[42.567, "o", "lts for ' + name + '' + ...);\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mImpact\u001b[m: An attacker can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the victim's browser by providing a malicious script in the \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mname\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\r\nparameter.\r\n- \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Sanitize user input or use a templating engine that automatically escapes output.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m3. Vulnerable Dependencies (High)\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mexpress@4.16.0\u001b[m: Outdated version with known security vulnerabilities.\r\n- \u001b[1mlodash@4.17.4\u001b[m: This version is vulnerable to \u001b[1mPrototype Pollution\u001b[m (CVE-2018-16487, CVE-2019-1000001).\r\n- \u001b[1mmysql@2.14.0\u001b[m: Outdated version.\r\n- \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Update all dependencies to their latest stable versions using \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mnpm update\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m or \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mnpm install [package]@latest\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m4. Broken Authentication / Sensitive Data Exposure (Medium)\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mHardcoded Credentials\u001b[m: The database connection uses hardcoded credentials (\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33muser: 'root', password: 'root'\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m).\r\n- \u001b[1mPlaintext Passwords\u001b[m: T"]
[42.567, "o", "he \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mlogin\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m function suggests passwords are stored in plaintext in the database.\r\n- \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Use environment variables for credentials and implement strong password hashing (e.g., Argon2 or bcrypt).\r\n"]
